  "source": "EAMCET 2007 (Medical)",
  "question": "A body of mass $m$ is raised from the surface of the earth to a height $nR$ ($R$ is the radius of the earth). The magnitude of the change in the gravitational potential energy of the body is ($g$ = acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the earth)",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\dfrac{n}{n + 1}\\right)mgR$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\dfrac{n - 1}{n}\\right)mgR$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{mgR}{n}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{mgR}{n - 1}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$\\Delta U = GMm\\left(\\frac{1}{R} - \\frac{1}{R + nR}\\right) = \\frac{GMm}{R}\\cdot\\frac{n}{n + 1} = \\left(\\frac{n}{n + 1}\\right)mgR$$\nusing $GM = gR^2$.",
